      {
        "id": 62821,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-13T18:56:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Spiff has been beaten down enough that he isn't going to raise a stink about interstellar recipe robots. &nbsp;I give up, already.</p><p>I am a little confused by the Kickstarter update though. &nbsp;There were two probes, one turned into the Omega Singularity, but I'm not clear on what happened to the other one. &nbsp;The update says it was \"memorialized in a shrine to peace\", which should mean that a shrine to peace was built to memorialize it, and therefore it's still buzzing around someplace. &nbsp;However, maybe they meant to say \"enshrined in a shrine to peace\", which would indicate that it was physically installed in the shrine and therefore it's not still buzzing around somewhere. &nbsp;So, is the Omega Singularity the only boss recipe (sigh) robot out there, or is there <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4JVcvR7IM0\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">another</a>?</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
