      {
        "id": 62831,
        "name": "Michael Vognild",
        "username": "Michael_Vognild",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/michael_vognild/{size}/2693_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-25T07:08:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So-- who piloted the Exogorth and the Sarlacc in Star Wars? &nbsp;Anybody?<br><br>Oh, yeah. &nbsp;I guess they were just really, really dangerous space creatures, and not ships. &nbsp;Mynocks still baffle me, but they were a cool, unexpected threat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Not every creature has a pilot, and not all creatures are 'ships' in the classical sense, though it's more elegant to collectively refer to all threats in space as a 'ship' rather than \"Opposition Opponent Beast/Construct Thingy.\"</p>",
